on","bytes":2173289,"shapes":549,"good_to_zoom":30},{"kind":"school","file":"layers/school.json","bytes":307705,"shapes":89,"good_to_zoom":11.8}],"school":{"files":"school/<id>.json"},"notes":{"lines":"Every precinct line is the State Board of Elections' (its file of August 24, 2026), generalised by at most 1.5 metres and set on a grid of 0.00001 degree (about a metre). A point within a few metres of a line can fall on either side of it.","precincts":"A shape is a precinct as the county board of elections drew it. The county board of elections is the authority on which precinct an address is in.","districts":"Each precinct's districts are the contests on its November 3, 2026 ballot, from the State Board of Elections' own table. The plans in force for 2026 are S.L. 2025-95 (cd); S.L. 2023-146 (senate); S.L. 2023-149 (house): the congressional lines are the 2025 plan, not the 2024 lines. Where the table puts a precinct in two districts of one kind (a split precinct), the plan's own lines say which holds more of it; split gives the shares. A district's outline here is made of whole precincts.","places":"North Carolina's cities, towns and villages, by the Census Bureau's 2025 lines. A precinct's mcd is the place holding half or more of it (absent outside every one); mcd_all lists every place it reaches where it reaches more than one or lies partly outside: to say which place a point is in, ask the mcd layer, not the precinct.","commissioners":"Commissioner districts are drawn where a county elects commissioners by district on this ballot (29 counties), made of the precincts whose ballot carries that district's contest; a precinct whose ballot carries two districts' contests (a split precinct) is drawn in both and names both in com_all, since no file of the district lines was read to say which part votes where. Where every precinct of a county votes on each district's seat, the commissioners are elected countywide from residence districts and no district is drawn; supervisor_plans names those counties.","judicial":"The judicial layer draws the district court districts with a contest on this ballot. Prosecutorial (district attorney) and superior court districts are not drawn: each precinct names its own (da, sup), from its ballot.","school":"School board areas are the precincts whose ballot carries the board's contests, from the State Board of Elections' table: a board appears only where it has a seat on this ballot, and a board's area is made of whole precincts. A precinct can be on two boards' ballots.","polling":"Polling places are the State Board of Elections' list for November 3, 2026, one place a precinct; the one-stop early voting sites, where any voter of the county may vote early, follow them.","authority":"For which precinct and districts an address is in, and where to vote, the county board of elections and the State Board of Elections' voter search are the authority.","precinct_ids":"A precinct's id is the county's five-digit code and the Board's precinct code (37183-01-07 is Wake County precinct 01-07)."},"sources":[{"id":"nc-sbe-precincts-20260824","agency":"North Carolina State Board of Elections","title":"Precincts, August 24, 2026 (SBE_PRECINCTS_20260824, shapefile)","about":"Every precinct of the 100 counties as the county boards drew them, the newest precinct file the Board has published (posted August 28, 2026). Drawn in the North Carolina State Plane and turned back into longitude and latitude here.","url":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/?prefix=ShapeFiles/","file":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/ShapeFiles/Precinct/SBE_PRECINCTS_20260824.zip","published":"2026-08-28","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"71f2a6a4d6601b44a0d3cfd4228dd51b199cb8ccb233d6e585bb4701c50cbe2e","rows":2625},{"id":"nc-sbe-results-pct-20261103","agency":"North Carolina State Board of Elections","title":"Precinct results file for the November 3, 2026 general election, before any vote was counted (results_pct_20261103)","about":"Every contest on every precinct's ballot (the file lists each contest in each precinct, with no votes yet). Each precinct's congressional, legislative, court, prosecutorial, commissioner, council, school board, soil and water and sanitary districts are the contests it holds.","url":"https://www.ncsbe.gov/results-data","file":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/ENRS/2026_11_03/results_pct_20261103.zip","published":"2026-10-05","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"a0a046b2878157904343e9053f747094c7230a8d5c0e2e80359e264071ac73fe","rows":2626},{"id":"nc-plan-cd","agency":"North Carolina State Board of Elections","title":"U.S. House of Representatives plan, S.L. 2025-95 (shapefile)","about":"The congressional plan enacted in October 2025, the 14 districts for the 2026 elections (not the 2024 lines). Laid over the precincts to settle split precincts and to check the Board's table.","url":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/?prefix=ShapeFiles/","file":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/ShapeFiles/USCongress/SL%202025-95%20-%20Shapefile.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"c21e18d29a0f6dd52636c866ca3b05295a0757c6d6d98ee42ffa0b2eee795897","rows":14},{"id":"nc-plan-senate","agency":"North Carolina State Board of Elections","title":"State Senate plan, S.L. 2023-146 (shapefile)","about":"The 50 Senate districts enacted in 2023, in force for 2026. Laid over the precincts to settle split precincts and to check the Board's table.","url":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/?prefix=ShapeFiles/","file":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/ShapeFiles/LegislativeDistricts/Shapefiles/Senate/SL%202023-146%20Senate%20-%20Shapefile.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"0e1bd6d97e3ce1dcb42e0b9b47cae6b5e82086ebafcded54e6b96bb7287b16f8","rows":50},{"id":"nc-plan-house","agency":"North Carolina State Board of Elections","title":"State House plan, S.L. 2023-149 (shapefile)","about":"The 120 House districts enacted in 2023, in force for 2026. Laid over the precincts to settle split precincts and to check the Board's table.","url":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/?prefix=ShapeFiles/","file":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/ShapeFiles/LegislativeDistricts/Shapefiles/House/SL%202023-149%20House%20-%20Shapefile.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"3b2e69226c528f18a21cb75dcb9de7f196bf105898efff55e73ef8faa365e75e","rows":120},{"id":"nc-sbe-precinct-names-20260303","agency":"North Carolina State Board of Elections","title":"Sorted precinct results of the March 3, 2026 primary (precinct code and name only)","about":"The precincts' names, read from the code and name columns of the Board's sorted results, one file per county.","url":"https://www.ncsbe.gov/results-data","file":"https://dl.ncsbe.gov/ENRS/2026_03_03/results_precinct_sort/<COUNTY>_PRECINCT_SORT.txt","fetched":"2026-10-17","rows":2633},{"id":"nc-census-cb-2024-counties","agency":"U.S. Census Bureau","title":"Cartographic boundary file 2024, counties (cb_2024_us_county_500k.zip)","about":"Read only to check that every precinct lies in the county it is filed under, and that each polling place lies in its county.","url":"https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/GENZ2024/shp/cb_2024_us_county_500k.zip","fetched":"2026-09-26","sha256":"da4051717caec55c75e3748c3608c2a3dbde8d1ff401bbaf4f952e3c3fb63ef1","rows":100},{"id":"nc-census-tiger-2025-places","agency":"U.S. Census Bureau","title":"TIGER/Line Shapefiles 2025, places, North Carolina (tl_2025_37_place.zip)","about":"City, town and village limits as the Bureau had them on January 1, 2025, from the municipalities' own reports; incorporated places only.","url":"https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/TIGER2025/PLACE/tl_2025_37_place.zip","fetched":"2026-10-17","sha256":"c6b8dabd4c953bb44dd4201b34eae83dceeb880055e1c4efd00faa43c272ea79","rows":549}]}